# Renault 19 phase 1 five-door hatchback, 1989-1992.
#
# The first-generation Renault 19 in its phase-1 form. On sale in Britain from
# 1989 (the model was launched in Europe in late 1988) and replaced by the phase
# 2 facelift in late 1992; the range ran to 1996, when the Megane replaced it.
# https://www.renault.co.uk/ (Renault 19 model page, cited in the reference pack)
#
# Dimensions 4.156 x 1.694 x 1.412 m, wheelbase 2.540 m. Source: the reference
# pack's notes, from the Renault 19 dimension box. The hull measures 4.156 m
# on a 2.540 m wheelbase (61.1 per cent) and 1.694 m wide; mirrors extend
# beyond.
#
# Shape reference: the pack has no true side elevation. The flank was built
# from a front-left three-quarter of a red car, a front-right three-quarter of
# a grey 1989 GTS and a rear-left view of the red car, with the wheel centres
# fixed by the published ratio; the model was compared at each photograph's
# actual angle and a true elevation was rendered for coherence.
#
# The phase-1 front is the smooth body-coloured badge panel with the Renault
# diamond, a separate narrow grille slot just above the bumper and the
# horizontal slats in the lower bumper intake — not the phase-2 nose, which
# merges the grille into the lamp line. The build brief originally described a
# full-width slatted grille; the builder checked the photographs and was right,
# and the photographed form is what is modelled.
#
# Colours: no British-market colour names were established for the 19. No
# Renault UK brochure, price list or press release with a colour chart was
# found, so the objects carry plain colour names rather than invented ones:
# white, red, blue and grey. Weights white 3, red 3, blue 2, grey 2, total 10,
# provisional pending the central rebase.
#
# Speed 175 km/h, the 1.4-litre car's quoted maximum. Comfort 70/435, on the
# line 330 + 1.5 x 70: a roomy, quiet family hatchback for 1989. Classes 0,1.
#
# Dates are road presence: 1989 intro, retires staggered 2001-2004 on a twelve-
# to fifteen-year tail.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/renault-19-phase1.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/renault-19-phase1.dae (91 objects). References:
# citycars/references/renault-19-phase1/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: the nose is flatter and more slab-like than the
# photographs and the front corners and arches are faceted; the rear is squarer
# than the real car's rounded hatch, and the painted centre panel between the
# tail lamps is retained as photographed. The top view confirms a continuous
# painted roof. At 128 px the flat bonnet, the separate grille slot and the
# sloping hatch read as the phase-1 19.

obj=citycar
name=Renault19Phase1(White)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=3
intro_year=1989
intro_month=1
retire_year=2004
retire_month=6
speed=175
class=0,1
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=70
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=435

